statement:
Call a natural number $n$ faithful if there exist natural numbers $a < b < c$ such that $a \mid b$, $b \mid c$, and $n = a + b + c$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] Show that all but a finite number of natural numbers are faithful.
\item[(ii)] Find the sum of all natural numbers which are not faithful.
\end{enumerate}
